Phase OS-17: Kernel Power Management - 3 new AArch64 assembly kernel modules:

1. kernel/power_cpufreq.asm (CPU Frequency Scaling)
   - Base ID: 913
   - Dynamic CPU frequency and voltage scaling for power efficiency
   - Features: frequency table management, governor selection (performance, powersave, ondemand, conservative), voltage regulation, thermal throttling, transition latency tracking, per-core frequency control
   - Data structures: cpufreq_policy_t (cpu_id, min_freq, max_freq, cur_freq, governor, voltage), cpufreq_table_t (freq_count, freq_list)
   - API: power_cpufreq_init, power_cpufreq_set_governor, power_cpufreq_set_freq, power_cpufreq_get_freq, power_cpufreq_get_temp, power_cpufreq_stats, power_cpufreq_throttle, power_cpufreq_restore
   - Capacity: 8 CPU cores, 16 frequency levels each, 4 governors
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style (stp/ldp frame, .global exports, .bss for state)

2. kernel/power_sleep.asm (Sleep State Management)
   - Base ID: 914
   - System sleep state transitions (suspend, hibernate, standby)
   - Features: sleep state selection, wakeup alarm setup, device suspend/resume ordering, RTC alarm management, sleep statistics, sleep entry/exit latency tracking
   - Data structures: sleep_state_t (state_id, entry_time, exit_time, wakeup_source, devices_suspended), sleep_config_t (default_state, wakeup_mask, rtc_alarm)
   - API: power_sleep_init, power_sleep_enter(state_id), power_sleep_exit, power_sleep_set_wakeup(device_id), power_sleep_rtc_alarm(seconds), power_sleep_stats, power_sleep_get_state, power_sleep_resume_devices
   - Capacity: 4 sleep states (S1 standby, S2 stop, S3 suspend-to-RAM, S4 hibernate), 32 wakeup sources
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style

3. kernel/power_thermal.asm (Thermal Management)
   - Base ID: 915
   - Thermal zone monitoring and cooling device management
   - Features: thermal zone tracking, temperature trip points, passive/active cooling policies, CPU throttling coordination, fan speed control, emergency shutdown, thermal statistics
   - Data structures: thermal_zone_t (zone_id, temperature, trip_hot, trip_crit, cooling_dev, trend), cooling_device_t (dev_id, type, cur_state, max_state)
   - API: power_thermal_init, power_thermal_register_zone(zone_id, trip_hot, trip_crit), power_thermal_get_temp(zone_id), power_thermal_register_cooling(dev_id, type), power_thermal_set_cooling(dev_id, state), power_thermal_stats, power_thermal_emergency_check
   - Capacity: 8 thermal zones, 16 cooling devices, 4 trip points per zone
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style

Build all 3 kernel modules with:
  clang --target=aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu -c -O2 -o kernel/<name>.o kernel/<name>.asm

